# Regenerated every cycle and never meaningfully diffs against the prior
# version (binary, no delta compression) -- committing it each run grew
# .git to >1GB over time and helped trigger the 2026-11-10 OOM incident
# that took the whole VM's cron down. Still rendered locally by
# visualize.py for anyone who wants to look at it on disk; just no longer
# tracked in git. data/history.csv and models/baselines.json still commit
# every cycle, so this doesn't affect the contribution graph.
